# rule.require.domain-discovery-for-term-proposals

## .what
whenever you intend to propose a new term to a domain distillate (a new dobj or dop added to the domain's shared vocabulary), back the proposal with domain discovery
do not propose a term you have not discovered

## .why
- a term proposed without discovery drifts, overloads, or duplicates an extant concept
- discovery surfaces attributes, states, relationships before they harden in the distillate
- terms from the domain compose; terms invented at the keyboard do not
- a distillate is shared vocabulary — a bad term there costs every reader and reference downstream

## .when it applies
| applies | does not apply |
|---------|----------------|
| propose a new dobj to the distillate (noun not yet named) | reuse/extend an extant discovered term |
| propose a new dop to the distillate (verb not yet performed) | pure rename of a discovered term |
| a new bounded concept enters the vocabulary | incidental non-domain code |

## .what it requires
before a term proposal enters the distillate:
1. run at least one discovery move (howto.domain-discovery) to back the term — premier tactics: dimensional decomposition + scenario timeline narration
2. confirm against ubiqlang rules — no synonym, no ambiguous overload
3. record discovered attributes, states, refs, and forbidden combinations as invariants
the discovery is the evidence behind the proposal; a term without it is a guess, not a distillate entry

## .the caveat
discovery is proportionate — an obvious dobj needs a quick vet, not a full matrix
the mandate: do not propose a domain term in a vacuum; anchor it in the domain first

## .enforcement
- term proposed to the distillate with no discovery that turns out a synonym/overload = blocker
- proposed dobj with no account of attributes/states/refs = nitpick
- proposed dobj/dop that spans variants, entered with no dimensional walk = nitpick (rule.require.dimensional-decomposition)

## .see also
- howto.domain-discovery.md — what it is and how to do it
- howto.dimensional-decomposition.md — a premier discovery tactic
- rule.require.persist-domain-term-evidence — persist the discovery evidence long-term
- rule.require.ubiqlang — vet the proposed term
